es in the face of impossible odds  as I often do please allow me to read a  few lines from the poem If by Roger  Kipling  if you can keep your head when all about  you are losing theirs and blaming it on  you  if you can trust yourself and all men  doubt you but make allowance for their  doubting too  if you can wait and not be tired by  waiting or being lied about don't deal  in lies or being hated don't give way to  hating and yet don't look too good don't  talk too wise  even this very poem is mocking my over  romantic Ridiculousness as I read it the  meta irony is not lost on me my friends  I'm a silly little kid trying to do a  bit of good in this world  thank you for having my back through all  of it all of my mistakes  thank you for the love  this is the Lex Friedman podcast  um  to support it  please check out our sponsors in the  description and now dear friends
 

